This i18n export shouldn't be exported from `main.ts`

```ts
const getI18n = (messages = {}) => {
  return createI18n({
    legacy: false,
    formatFallbackMessages: true,
    silentFallbackWarn: false,
    locale: 'en',
    messages,
  });
};

export const i18n = getI18n();
```

A better solution would be to use provide/inject here:

Provide `i18n` from `main.ts`

```ts
// ...
const i18n = getI18n();

// ...
app.provide('i18n', i18n);

```

Inject it in hooks/components:

```ts
// ...
const i18n = inject('i18n');
// ...
```

I figured out a simple way to ensure that the Rebuild icon does not appear. It's already in the database: `worksite_worksites_data.phase_id`. All we need to do is sort by `phase_id`. phase_id 4 is "cleanup," while phase_id 5 is "LTR" or "Rebuild" I believe. Instead of hard-coding "4" (which is quite arbitrary), I added a new column called `portal_portals.default_phase_id`. Basically, the map shows worksites with the `default_phase_id` for that portal, and anything other than the default is de-prioritized.

Here are the basic steps:
- [x] Run the code below to create and populate `portal_portals.default_phase_id`
- [ ] The code below also includes a missing column, `portal_portals_history.parent_id`.
- [ ] Update the work icon algorithm to de-prioritize work_types where `worksite_work_types.phase_id <> portal_portals.default_phase_id` UNLESS: 1 The organization claimed the work_type, or 2. The only available work_type.phase_id values do not equal default_phase_id.
```
ALTER TABLE IF EXISTS public.portal_portals ADD COLUMN default_phase_id integer;
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.portal_portals.default_phase_id IS 'fkey to incident_phases.id. This foreign key is a part of the algorithm to determine which work_type icons appear on the map. Any work_type icons not in the default_phase_id are de-prioritized to aid with clarity.';

ALTER TABLE IF EXISTS public.portal_portals
    ADD CONSTRAINT default_phase_id_fkey FOREIGN KEY (default_phase_id)
    REFERENCES public.incident_phases (id) MATCH SIMPLE
    ON UPDATE NO ACTION
    ON DELETE NO ACTION
    NOT VALID;

ALTER TABLE IF EXISTS public.portal_portals_history ADD COLUMN default_phase_id integer;
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.portal_portals.default_phase_id IS 'fkey to incident_phases.id. This foreign key is a part of the algorithm to determine which work_type icons appear on the map. Any work_type icons not in the default_phase_id are de-prioritized to aid with clarity.';

ALTER TABLE IF EXISTS public.portal_portals_history
    ADD CONSTRAINT default_phase_id_fkey FOREIGN KEY (default_phase_id)
    REFERENCES public.incident_phases (id) MATCH SIMPLE
    ON UPDATE NO ACTION
    ON DELETE NO ACTION
    NOT VALID;

ALTER TABLE IF EXISTS public.portal_portals_history ADD COLUMN parent_id integer;
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.portal_portals_history.parent_id IS 'parent id of the portal being configured. A parent indicates that they operate on the same underlying database. They are essentially different views of the same data.';

ALTER TABLE IF EXISTS public.portal_portals_history
    ADD CONSTRAINT parent_id_fkey FOREIGN KEY (parent_id)
    REFERENCES public.portal_portals_history (id) MATCH SIMPLE
    ON UPDATE NO ACTION
    ON DELETE NO ACTION
    NOT VALID;


UPDATE portal_portals
SET default_phase_id = 4;

UPDATE portal_portals_history
SET default_phase_id = 4;
```

## Description

Replace this logic with reusable hook/util in the repo:

```ts
const ccuApi = useApi();
const fieldsToFetch = [
  'id',
  'name',
  'short_name',
  'active_phone_number',
  'start_at',
];
const { isDataLoading, data } = ccuApi(
  '/incidents?fields=id,name,short_name,active_phone_number&limit=200&sort=-start_at',
  {
    method: 'GET',
    params: {
      fields: fieldsToFetch.join(','),
      limit: 200,
      sort: '-start_at',
    },
  },
);
const incidentList = computed(() => data.value?.results);
function getIncidentPhoneNumbers(incident) {
  if (Array.isArray(incident.active_phone_number)) {
    return incident.active_phone_number
      .map((number) => formatNationalNumber(String(number)))
      .join(', ');
  }
  return formatNationalNumber(String(incident.active_phone_number));
}
function filterNumbers(item) {
  return item.filter((filterItem) => filterItem.active_phone_number);
}
```

